A hidden, experimental `--recursive-modules` option, requiring `--member-invariants`, begins recursion across module boundaries (https://github.com/erniecohen/dafny/issues/466). With it, the modules of a cycle of plain imports form a recursive module group. A cycle that goes through a `refines` or `replaces` clause, an abstract import, the binding of an inherited abstract import, or the nesting of a module in another is an error that names that edge; a replaceable module may not be in a group; and a program that has a group may not declare a codatatype. In this first stage the groups are computed and listed by `--show-hints`, and a group of more than one module is then rejected as not yet supported, so no program is accepted that was rejected before. A `.doo` library built with the option requires it of its clients; one built without it is unchanged. Without the option, every diagnostic is unchanged.
